## 7. Pre-Production Gates (⬜ the real 2-month engineering work)
- [⬜] **Simulators → real SNMP** (Task 2 strategic fix).
- [⬜] **Scale model:** Zabbix **proxies** per zone + drop per-ATM published-port model (current 1161–2500 range cannot reach 2,500 ATMs). Single listener per zone, ATM by IP/community/index.
- [⬜] Obtain + compile **real NCR & GRG MIBs**; build OID mapping table (sim OID ↔ real OID ↔ Zabbix item); commit to repo.
- [⬜] SNMP **v3** (authPriv) where ATMs support it; bank-specific community otherwise.
- [⬜] **ISO 8583** gateway validated against real switch messages (connection direction, variant, sample pcaps) — currently simulation-only.
- [⬜] **EJ delivery** method decided (central collector / network share / SFTP) + **PCI DSS PAN masking** verified on real logs.
- [⬜] Reconcile fleet count (Task 1 blocker).

## 8. Deployment (⬜ once server + ATM access provided)
- [⬜] Build per-VM compose files (5 VMs RHEL 9) — structure exists in migration guide §4.
- [⬜] Deploy UAT → Production in order (DB → Zabbix → OpenSearch → Grafana/GLPI → Gateway).
- [⬜] Import Zabbix templates/hosts/media types; push Grafana dashboards via API.
- [⬜] **Pilot wave (10–50 ATMs)** over SNMP; **parallel run vs NetXMS** 2–4 weeks; validate parity.
- [⬜] Phased fleet expansion by zone after pilot is trusted.
- [⬜] Backup/DR (pg_dump daily off-server, OpenSearch snapshots, restore tested).

## 9. Honest gaps vs NetXMS (accept or mitigate — communicate to stakeholders)
- [⬜] **ATM screen screenshot/screencast:** not over SNMP. Mitigate: out of BRD scope; or source via vendor console.
- [⬜] **Link-loss data caching:** SNMP gaps during ATM outage. Mitigate: rely on Switch EJ feed for transaction record; accept brief telemetry gaps.
- [⬜] **Remote actions (reboot/card-eject):** not in BRD scope; SNMP alone cannot. Accept.

